Spring Boot
1.Check java and maven version : java -version , mvn -version
2. Create a spring boot project using Spring initializr adding Spring Web as dependency
3. Unzip the downloaded project and navigate to the project folder
4. Create a spring boot application
Create this file : src/main/java/com/example/demo/HelloController.java
package com.example.demo;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;
@RestController
public class HelloController {
@GetMapping("/")
public String hello() {
return "Hello, Spring Boot by 24WH1A05C5_SAMEEKSHA!";
}}
5. Run the application : mvn spring-boot:run
6.Verify in browser : http:localhost:8080

Karate
1.Create a Karate project
mvn archetype:generate \
-DarchetypeGroupId=com.intuit.karate \
-DarchetypeArtifactId=karate-archetype \
-DarchetypeVersion=1.4.1 \
-DgroupId=com.example \
-DartifactId=karate-demo \
-DinteractiveMode=false
2. Open the project : cd karate-demo
3. Run the sample Karate test : mvn test
4. View reports : xdg-open target/karate-reports/karate-summary.html
